\title{From reflection generation to Pin and Spin}

\p{One reflection can enlarge the fixed subspace of an orthogonal
transformation. Iterating this correction proves reflection generation and
makes the unnormalized Lipschitz action onto the orthogonal group. Passing to
the norm-one Pin and Spin carriers requires scalar normalization: determinant
parity controls evenness, while the spinor norm measures the remaining
obstruction over a general field.}

